.TH YR "1" "November 2026" "YARA-X" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yr \- pattern matching and malware research tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yr
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] <\fICOMMAND\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
YARA\-X is the Rust-based rewrite of YARA, the pattern matching swiss army knife
aimed at helping malware researchers identify and classify malware samples.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
Scan a file or directory
.TP
.B compile
Compile rules to binary form
.TP
.B dump
Show the data produced by YARA modules for a file
.TP
.B fmt
Format YARA source files
.TP
.B fix
Utilities for fixing source code
.TP
.B completion
Output shell completion code for the specified shell
.TP
.B deps
Show rule dependencies
.TP
.B help
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR <\fICONFIG_FILE\fR>
Specifies a config file which controls the behavior of YARA\-X. If no config
file is specified, \fI${HOME}/.yara\-x.toml\fR is used. If it does not exist,
the default options are applied. See
\fIhttps://virustotal.github.io/yara\-x/docs/cli/config\-file/\fR for supported
options.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with '\-h')
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SEE ALSO
Full CLI documentation: \fIhttps://virustotal.github.io/yara\-x/docs/cli/\fR
.SH AUTHOR
Victor M. Alvarez <vmalvarez@virustotal.com>
